# Nougat OCR stub — lucid100-pprm-small-rna-deinococcus

**Status:** placeholder. Nougat OCR (facebookresearch/nougat) was NOT run against `artifacts/paper.pdf` in the 2026-06-09/2026-06-22/2026-07-06 passes.

## Rationale for placeholder

The paper is Nature Scientific Reports OA (CC BY 4.0) and provided as machine-readable text via the OA XML endpoint; `artifacts/paper.txt` already contains the extracted plain-text body used by all reproduction analysis. There was no evidence-gathering need for Nougat-quality math/table OCR because:

1. Numerical claims audited in this reproduction (L2FC, padj) come from `supplement1.xlsx` (S1–S9 tables), not from the PDF body.
2. The PDF text extraction was clean for prose sections (no math-heavy sections in this paper — it is an experimental biology paper, not theoretical).
3. Figure content (EMSA gels, Northern blots, survival curves) is inherently not text-recoverable and would not benefit from OCR.

## When to actually run Nougat

Run Nougat on `artifacts/paper.pdf` if any of the following becomes needed:

- Cross-verification of Methods section formulas (e.g. IntaRNA scoring, statistical model specification) against the extracted text.
- Table extraction from the PDF body (Tables 1, 2 of the main text) if the supplement XLSX becomes unavailable.
- Machine-readable capture of figure captions for downstream LLM analysis.

## How to run (reference command)

```bash
# From slot dir, on uicgpu or a GPU-capable host
source .venv-nougat/bin/activate  # requires nougat-ocr 0.1.17+
nougat artifacts/paper.pdf -o extraction/ --model 0.1.0-base --markdown
# Output: extraction/paper.mmd (this file replaced with actual OCR)
```

